 {
  "object": "block",
  "id": "cd690cb4-b519-4d07-ab2d-73d5776c8f06",
  "parent": {
   "type": "page_id",
   "page_id": "36694183-19f3-801f-9c87-f2dbf7041ddb"
  },
  "created_time": "2026-06-12T01:43:00.000Z",
  "last_edited_time": "2026-06-15T12:43:00.000Z",
  "created_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "last_edited_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "114d872b-594c-8174-9474-0002954cf668"
  },
  "has_children": false,
  "in_trash": false,
  "type": "paragraph",
  "paragraph": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "When the HTTP Node returns an error instead of data, Agent Node B without explicit failure handling either fabricates a status or writes an incorrect value to Flow State. Flow State is a runtime key-value store shared among nodes in a single execution. A fabricated value written to ",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "When the HTTP Node returns an error instead of data, Agent Node B without explicit failure handling either fabricates a status or writes an incorrect value to Flow State. Flow State is a runtime key-value store shared among nodes in a single execution. A fabricated value written to ",
     "href": null
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "$flow.state.status_response",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": true,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "$flow.state.status_response",
     "href": null
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": " is immediately available to every downstream node that reads from that key and the contamination is structural and immediate.",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": " is immediately available to every downstream node that reads from that key and the contamination is structural and immediate.",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "icon": null,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
 {
  "object": "block",
  "id": "9ab0e079-ae27-4b54-8cbc-c958c3d0a2fd",
  "parent": {
   "type": "page_id",
   "page_id": "36694183-19f3-801f-9c87-f2dbf7041ddb"
  },
  "created_time": "2026-06-12T01:43:00.000Z",
  "last_edited_time": "2026-06-15T12:43:00.000Z",
  "created_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "231d872b-594c-81f2-a375-0002b8783aca"
  },
  "last_edited_by": {
   "object": "user",
   "id": "114d872b-594c-8174-9474-0002954cf668"
  },
  "has_children": false,
  "in_trash": false,
  "type": "paragraph",
  "paragraph": {
   "rich_text": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": {
      "content": "In Sprint 3, the Loop Node will handle retry logic for failed HTTP calls. The Loop Node's Max Loop Count parameter defines the maximum number of times the loop can execute within a single workflow run, safeguarding against infinite cycles. The default value is 5. Without a configured exit path when the limit is reached, the loop terminates without returning a meaningful response.",
      "link": null
     },
     "annotations": {
      "bold": false,
      "italic": false,
      "strikethrough": false,
      "underline": false,
      "code": false,
      "color": "default"
     },
     "plain_text": "In Sprint 3, the Loop Node will handle retry logic for failed HTTP calls. The Loop Node's Max Loop Count parameter defines the maximum number of times the loop can execute within a single workflow run, safeguarding against infinite cycles. The default value is 5. Without a configured exit path when the limit is reached, the loop terminates without returning a meaningful response.",
     "href": null
    }
   ],
   "icon": null,
   "color": "default"
  },
  "archived": false
 },
